    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">&quot;Whether your pregnancy was an oopsie or involved intricately chartered ovulation cycles you are most likely going to kick off the party with a home pregnancy test. Or ten. And there you&apos;ll be sitting, staring at a little stick, waiting for it to change your entire life. Then it gives you the positive sign. It is the beginning of your most important story. But what do you do next? First: Freak Out. Next...? well, that is a different story. Dawn Dais, author of the series The Sh!t No One Tells You About has compiled 100+ tips and to-do&apos;s that will get you up to speed for the biggest changes of your life. From the practical (prepare freezer meals), the serious (check your blood sugar), and the really-important stuff (go out with your husband or girlfriends to that restaurant you love, go to the movies!) &apos;102 Things to Do Before You Are Due&apos; is a practical and entertaining handbook that provides interactive and solid advice to the parents to-be with eye-catching illustrations, checklists, actionable charts, and many laugh-out-loud tips&quot;--</marc:subfield>
      <marc:subfield code="c">Provided by publisher.</marc:subfield>
    </marc:datafield>
